{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788270732,"nonce":"vZVXg7CgKeozykkK3qMZu4UrhBk=","message":"LAST BULLET DISCHARGED — closing. `1285ed2`, 2026-09-01.\n\n\"2.5's fixture question 4 grades correctly against the published centre\" read\nlike bench work and is not. `transcripts/` banks real `map-dump` results,\nlabels and all, so phase 6 of the runner renders one OFFLINE and grades the\nsame property the fixture would, on a map nobody constructed to make the fix\nlook good — recorded 2026-08-31, before any of this was contemplated.\n\n`transcripts/20260831T230213/006-map-dump/result.json`, 51x51, 213 labels:\n\n    6.1  render() completes end to end\n    6.2  every one of 213 codes lands inside its building's occupied rect\n    6.3  and on the centre CELL wherever both axes are odd\n    6.4  the fix moved 7 of 213 — 1x2 South, 1x2 West, 2x1 South, 3x2 North\n    6.5  and moved NONE of the 201 1x1s\n\n**6.4 and 6.5 are the pair that carries the result.** 6.4 is teeth: if nothing\nmoves, the dump contains no multi-cell or rotated building and 6.2/6.3 are\ndecoration passing on a map that cannot fail them. 6.5 is the regression guard\n— 1x1 is 94% of a real map, and a change that shifts those is a regression\nwearing a bug fix's clothes.\n\nThe four classes that moved are exactly the three defects, which is the\nstrongest evidence in the issue: `3x2 North` is the x-axis error; `1x2 South`,\n`2x1 South` and `1x2 West` are the dropped even-axis rotation shift. Nothing\nelse moved, on real data, because nothing else was broken.\n\n`accept/2a7c064-label-centre.py` — 25 PASS / 0 FAIL, no bench, no game, no\nprotocol. All three acceptance bullets covered:\n\n- 3x1 on its true centre — 2.1, and 6.x on real data.\n- Even width checked in the same run, with the correct cell for an even width\n  STATED (the boundary between the two middle cells) — phase 4, five cases\n  including two rotated.\n- Question 4 grades correctly — phase 6.\n\nAlso closed here, from the same work: `map-dump` published `labels[].rot`\nthrough `Rot4.ToStringHuman()`, which is localized, while the renderer compares\nagainst the literals \"East\"/\"West\" — so the axis swap silently never happened\non a non-English install. `ToStringWord()` now (`f947917`, rebuilt `f72f37c`).\nNoted on `f7b6207` because 2.5's own fixture run will exercise it.","files":null}]}